{
  "category": "Mushroom Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Burrows to suck tree roots. The mushrooms on its back grow by drawing nutrients from the bug host.",
      "version": "red"
    },
    {
      "text": "Burrows to suck tree roots. The mushrooms on its back grow by drawing nutrients from the bug host.",
      "version": "blue"
    },
    {
      "text": "Burrows under the ground to gnaw on tree roots. The mushrooms on its back absorb most of the nutrition.",
      "version": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is doused with mushroom spores when it is born. As its body grows, mushrooms sprout from its back.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "As its body grows large, oriental mushrooms named tochukaso start sprouting out of its back.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "The tochukaso growing on this POKéMON's back orders it to extract juice from tree trunks.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "PARAS has parasitic mushrooms growing on its back called tochukaso. They grow large by drawing nutrients from the BUG POKéMON host. They are highly valued as a medicine for extending life.",
